aphs\",\n        \"Levin Peres Wilmer Markov chains and mixing times cover time Matthews method\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_id\": \"positioning-family-asymptotics\",\n      \"section\": \"Background and Related Work\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"citation_intent\": \"benchmark_context\",\n      \"reason\": \"The Positioning paragraph says prior work derives 'asymptotics for specific families' but cites none. The Discussion then relies on such results without citations: random 3-regular and dense Erdos-Renyi graphs sit in the near-n ln n regime, and grid cover time may not follow a single power law. One to three citations for random-regular, random-graph and 2D-torus cover-time asymptotics would ground these statements and the choice of evaluated families. The story does not need to change.\",\n      \"anchor_text\": \"it derives bounds that hold for all graphs, or asymptotics for specific families\",\n      \"search_topics\": [\n        \"Cooper Frieze cover time of random regular graphs\",\n        \"Cooper Frieze cover time of sparse random graphs Erdos-Renyi giant component\",\n        \"Dembo Peres Rosen Zeitouni cover times for Brownian motion and random walks in two dimensions\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"failure_reason\": \"\"\n}\nEOF\npython3 -m json.tool draft_reference_gaps.json >/dev/null && echo ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3977,"cache_read_input_tokens":45352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3977,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62295646-bbb4-4220-8ef6-58680e3146b4","uuid":"be121ebb-58aa-4114-809f-5fda83505620","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:42:42.533Z","request_id":"req_011CgTEWMkw5aX